  "instructions": [
    "preheat oven to 400°f (200°c).",
    "cut the cantaloupe into wedges and roast in the oven for 20 minutes, or until caramelized.",
    "in a kadhai vessel, heat 1 tbsp of coconut oil over medium heat.",
    "add the onion and cook until softened, about 5 minutes.",
    "add the ginger, garlic, and garam masala, and cook for 1 minute, stirring constantly.",
    "add the cumin powder, coriander powder, cayenne pepper, salt, and black pepper, and cook for 1 minute, stirring constantly.",
    "add the red lentils, tomato puree, and 2 cups of water, and bring to a boil.",
    "reduce the heat to low and simmer for 15-20 minutes, or until the lentils are tender.",
    "add the roasted melon wedges to the kadhai vessel and simmer for an additional 2-3 minutes, or until heated through.",
    "taste and adjust the seasoning as needed.",
    "garnish with chopped fresh cilantro and serve hot."
  ],
